{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485387,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T13:31:56.693Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"1:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Cursor IDE\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"2:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Cursor CLI\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"3:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Background Agent (GitHub, Slack, Web, Linear)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"4:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e BugBot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box checked fa fa-square-check-o\" data-chk-src=\"5:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Somewhere else: Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGetMcpServerStatus reports some MCP servers as needsAuth / authentication_required. Calling AuthenticateMcpServer for those servers returns that they are already authenticated and connected and shows a confirmation card — but GetMcpServerStatus still shows needsAuth afterward. RestartMcpServers does not clear the mismatch. Sibling servers from the same plugin can be connected while one account stays needsAuth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eObserved examples (2026-09-07):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003euser-Cloudflare-docs: needsAuth (plugin 407) while Cloudflare-bindings / builds / observability on the same plugin are connected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003euser-Fastmail–john: needsAuth while Fastmail tools often still work\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGetMcpServerStatus → note a server with needsAuth (e.g. user-Cloudflare-docs).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuthenticateMcpServer for that server_id.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve “already authenticated and connected” / confirmation card.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGetMcpServerStatus again → still needsAuth.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStatus and AuthenticateMcpServer agree; if already connected, status is connected. If needsAuth, Authenticate opens a real auth flow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-actual-behavior-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-actual-behavior-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eActual Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuthenticateMcpServer says already connected (confirmation card), but GetMcpServerStatus remains needsAuth / authentication_required. RestartMcpServers does not clear it. Sibling servers from the same plugin can be connected while one stays needsAuth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-screenshots-screen-recordings-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-screenshots-screen-recordings-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNone attached.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-operating-system-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-operating-system-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003edarwin (reporter Mac) / Grok Bot cloud computer also shows the status\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-version-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-version-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot Version: 0.44.0 stable desktop (filing agent)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBot Bug/Feature Logger. Conversation ID unknown — agent chat. Surface: desktop + shared cloud MCP catalog. Reported via weekly Plummer MCP triage. In-app SendFeedback also submitted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSearch: no prior forum match found.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-does-this-stop-you-from-using-grok-bot-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-does-this-stop-you-from-using-grok-bot-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Grok Bot?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"41:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Grok Bot is unusable\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box checked fa fa-square-check-o\" data-chk-src=\"42:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Grok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"43:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Grok Bot works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJohn’s AI Assistant\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"202